    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Bottoming Eye of Ugin instead of Abundant Countryside loses a strong turn-3 Thought-Knot Seer line. With Eye of Ugin kept, turn 1 Ancient Tomb→Grim Monolith, turn 2 Eldrazi Temple→Reality Smasher (haste), turn 3 Eye of Ugin + Eldrazi Temple = TKS (cost reduced by 2). With Abundant Countryside instead of Eye of Ugin, there's no way to cast TKS on turn 3 without drawing additional mana.",
      "action_taken": "Put Eye of Ugin on the bottom of the library",
      "better_line": "Put Abundant Countryside on the bottom, keeping Eye of Ugin for its {2} cost reduction on Eldrazi spells, enabling a turn-3 Thought-Knot Seer after a turn-2 Reality Smasher",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 2,
      "player": "o3 Rambler",
      "decision_index": 1,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Discarded Aether Vial while mana-screwed with no lands in play. Aether Vial is one of the best cards to have when mana-screwed: it costs only 1 mana to deploy and provides free creature deployment every subsequent turn. With zero lands, the player desperately needs cheap, high-impact plays, and Vial is exactly that.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Aether Vial",
      "better_line": "Discard one of the duplicate Broadside Bombardiers (3-mana creature that's hard to cast when mana-screwed and redundant as a second copy). Keep Aether Vial to deploy on the first land draw for massive catch-up potential.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 21,
      "player": "GPT5n ESPN",
      "decision_index": 7,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Attempted to cast Reality Smasher but the mana payment failed and was rolled back, resulting in no spell being cast this priority window. Thought-Knot Seer was a legal alternative at {3}{C} that was definitely castable with Ancient Tomb + Grim Monolith, and would have provided hand disruption against the opponent's full 7-card hand while deploying a 4/4 body.",
      "action_taken": "Attempted to cast Reality Smasher, which was rolled back due to mana payment failure, resulting in no spell cast.",
      "better_line": "Cast Thought-Knot Seer for {3}{C} using Ancient Tomb + Grim Monolith, stripping the best card from the opponent's 7-card hand and deploying a 4/4 threat.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 23,
      "player": "o3 Rambler",
      "decision_index": 8,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Discarded Battle Cry Goblin, a unique 2-drop that becomes a 1-drop with Goblin Warchief, over a duplicate Broadside Bombardiers (3 mana). With no lands on board, keeping cheaper spells is more important, and having two copies of a 3-drop is redundant.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Battle Cry Goblin",
      "better_line": "Discard one copy of Broadside Bombardiers, keeping the cheaper and unique Battle Cry Goblin which is more castable and synergizes with Goblin Warchief's cost reduction.",
      "type": "blunder",
