      "player": "GPT5n ESPN",
      "decision_index": 18,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing City of Traitors instead of Cavern of Souls. Both lands provide enough mana to cast either Thought-Knot Seer or Reality Smasher this turn, but City of Traitors will be sacrificed when the next land is played, while Cavern of Souls (naming Eldrazi) would stay permanently and make Eldrazi spells uncounterable. The extra mana from City doesn't enable any additional plays this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Played City of Traitors",
      "better_line": "Play Cavern of Souls (naming Eldrazi) to have a permanent land that also makes Eldrazi uncounterable, then cast Thought-Knot Seer or Reality Smasher with the same available mana.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 68,
      "player": "o3 Rambler",
      "decision_index": 38,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Failed to activate Bloodstained Mire to fetch a Mountain, leaving them unable to cast any of the 8 cards in hand (all requiring red mana). With the opponent's board tapped, this was the critical window to start deploying Goblins like Skirk Prospector or Goblin Lackey. Instead, the entire turn is wasted while facing a 5/5 Reality Smasher.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out and passed priority without activating Bloodstained Mire.",
      "better_line": "Activate Bloodstained Mire to fetch a Mountain, then cast Skirk Prospector or Goblin Lackey to begin developing the board while the opponent's creatures are tapped.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 86,
      "player": "GPT5n ESPN",
      "decision_index": 43,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to crack Bloodstained Mire in response to Thought-Knot Seer on the stack. While they can still crack it after TKS resolves, doing it now is free and ensures they have a basic land on the battlefield (relevant against Wasteland, which the opponent could have). There's no reason not to activate it when given the chance.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out / no response, declining to activate Bloodstained Mire while Thought-Knot Seer is on the stack.",
      "better_line": "Activate Bloodstained Mire to fetch a Mountain, ensuring access to colored mana and protecting against potential Wasteland.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 97,
      "player": "GPT5n ESPN",
      "decision_index": 59,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Exiling Goblin Warchief over Munitions Expert with Thought-Knot Seer. Munitions Expert is a flash removal spell that can kill Reality Smasher or Thought-Knot Seer once the opponent has enough goblins on board. With two large Eldrazi dominating combat, the opponent's best path to staying in the game is removing those threats, not just deploying more small goblins. Without Munitions Expert, the opponent has very limited ways to interact with the 5/5 and 4/4.",
      "action_taken": "Exiled Goblin Warchief from opponent's hand",
      "better_line": "Exile Munitions Expert - it's the opponent's only clean instant-speed removal for Reality Smasher and Thought-Knot Seer, and removing the opponent's ability to answer the big Eldrazi is more impactful than slowing their goblin deployment by one mana and haste.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 101,
      "player": "o3 Rambler",
      "decision_index": 70,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to play a land during precombat main phase. Playing Wasteland and using it to destroy opponent's only land (Bloodstained Mire) would have cut the opponent off mana entirely while they're already behind on board. Preserving City of Traitors for one extra colorless mana is less valuable than mana-screwing the opponent.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without playing a land to preserve City of Traitors' double mana production.",
      "better_line": "Play Wasteland (sacrificing City of Traitors), then activate Wasteland to destroy opponent's Bloodstained Mire, cutting them off all mana sources while ahead on board with Reality Smasher and Thought-Knot Seer.",
      "type": "blunder",
